From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: h700: keep the speaker amplifier off at start

Every H700 board drives its speaker amplifier enable from PI5 (the
codec's allwinner,pa-gpios). Out of reset (power on, a reboot, a wake-up
from the universal standby) the pin floats while the amplifier is
already powered, which popped. The SPL drives it low right after the
GPIO init, level before direction, until Linux takes it.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -479,6 +479,17 @@
 	timer_init();
 	clock_init();
 	gpio_init();
+#ifdef CONFIG_NUUBOS_H700_VENDOR_DRAM
+	/*
+	 * Every H700 board drives its speaker amplifier enable from PI5 (the
+	 * codec's allwinner,pa-gpios). Out of reset (power on, a reboot, a
+	 * wake-up from the universal standby) the pin floats while the
+	 * amplifier is already powered, which pops: hold it off until Linux
+	 * takes it. Level first, then direction, so it never drives high.
+	 */
+	gpio_set_value(SUNXI_GPI(5), 0);
+	gpio_direction_output(SUNXI_GPI(5), 0);
+#endif
 
 	spl_init();
 	preloader_console_init();
